<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daehan seeks 28,000T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Daehan seeks 28,000T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd on Friday invited tenders to buy 28,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat, traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said the total amount would be split into four postions -- 14,200 tonnes of western white/soft white, 1,000 tonnes of western white (club minimum 15 percent), 3,300 tonnes of hard red winter (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 9,500 tonnes of dark northern spring (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Later, a Daehan official confirmed the company invited the tenders, saying shipment was set for between April 10 and May 10 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
